PRINCIPLE (campaign design's generator wins; the fun and scope critiques' metric wins). Waves stream sequentially (BeginWave: `at+=max(2,count*gap)+.8`, gap .78 s / .24 s swarm, 5 s breather), so raw counts mostly lengthen a level and fund themselves through kill rewards. Difficulty therefore comes from three dials, all authored in CarrotData.cs by `scripts/carrot-waves.mjs --write` (checked in; `--baseline` prints the frozen pre-retune arrays): (1) counts, moderate; (2) cadence: per-chapter spawn-gap scale, a 0.85 packet-overlap factor on pre-boss (p=2) and boss (p=3) levels from level 5, breathers 5/5/4/3/3/3 s by chapter; (3) per-enemy HP: old HPScale x (1 + .02(L-1) + .08 on boss levels + .05 on levels 1-2). Kill rewards, stipends and starting gold are unchanged. Measure = Pressure(L) = sum over packets of baseHP[kind] x count x HPScale(L) divided by stream seconds (sum of max(2,count x gap x overlap)+.8 per packet plus breathers), ordinary enemies only; bosses are a separate spike.

GENERATOR RULES (scripts/carrot-waves.mjs, deterministic from the OLD strings, which it keeps as `waves.baseline.json`): p=(L-1)%4, c=floor((L-1)/4). Count multiplier C: chapter 0 = [1.10,1.15,1.25,1.35][p]; chapters 1-5 = [1.15,1.20,1.30,1.40][p] + 0.02*min(c,3). Every packet n -> max(n+1, round(n*C)); boss packets stay 1; the FIRST packet of a kind on the level that introduces it stays verbatim (shell:3 on 3, moth:4 on 5, shaman:1 on 7, crystal:3 on 9, burrow:3 on 11), so first contact stays teachable. Injections: L>=5: wave floor(W/2) gets shell +(2+c); L>=7 and p>=2: the last two non-boss waves get shaman +(1+floor(c/2)); L>=9 and p>=2: the last non-boss wave gets crystal +(2+c); L>=11 and p>=1: wave W-3 gets burrow +(2+c); boss levels: the final wave gets shell +(3+c), dash +(4+c), moth +(3+c) from L8, crystal +(2+c) from L12, and wave W-2 gets swarm +(8+2c). GapScale(L) = [1.00,.95,.90,.85,.80,.78][c] applied to the .78/.24 gaps (boss gap 1.8 s unscaled); PacketOverlap(L) = .85 when p>=2 and L>=5, else 1; Breather(L) = 5 (c<2), 4 (c=2), 3 (c>=3); the early-call bonus stays min(6, remaining seconds). HPScale table (new): {1.05,1.23,1.35,1.65,1.67,1.93,2.18,2.62,2.67,3.01,3.36,4.03,4.03,4.28,4.54,5.11,5.08,5.36,5.64,6.28,6.23,6.53,6.84,7.55} then challenge entries {2.62 (=HPScale(8)), 6.28 (=HPScale(20)), 8.68 (=HPScale(24)*1.15)}. Spawn: `hp*=HPScale(level)*PressureScale(level)`; Pressure[27] defaults to 1, the only sanctioned post-tuning knob (floor .85; .80 allowed on 8-12), every non-1 entry listed in balance-results.md.

